<title>CHILE: Cruz Blanca sells unit to local group.</title>
<headline>Cruz Blanca sells unit to local group.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean financial holding company Cruz Blanca SA on Friday said it sold its health and general insurance unit, known as CB Prevision y Seguros, to a local group of investors for $200 million.</p>
<p>The unit was sold to a group of investors represented by Juan Hurtado Vicuna and Maximiliano Grez Dominguez, said Cruz Blanca CEO Albert Cussen.</p>
<p>Cruz Blanca will hold a stockholders meeting January 17 to approve a reorganization of the comapny before the sale takes place, he said.</p>
<p>-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212</p>
